The camera-rail helper manually adapts algorithms from OpenAgents camera_rig.rs
and film_shot.rs at revision 83fe8b7f6b3cd437ae9b7af213cf9f04875dd793.

Source: https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents
License: Apache License, Version 2.0; see LICENSE in this directory.

Integer timing, transported up vectors, and roll support are Aethyrforge additions.

The character-camera helper manually adapts FollowCamera from
crates/verse-gfx/src/camera.rs at the same revision. The Rust walking kernel adapts
movement constants and rules from crates/verse-world/src/social/controller.rs,
re-exported by crates/verse/src/controller.rs and used by Everglade.

Aethyrforge keeps its -Z-forward coordinate system, 0.3-meter walking radius,
fixed simulation ticks, and owned building collision. Static triangle contacts,
the bounded spatial index, collision queries, and measured movement velocity are
Aethyrforge additions. The orbit starts six meters away for the town. First-
person transition, zoom hysteresis, collision pull-in, and eased return follow
Verse's camera behavior.
